Let $z=x+i y\therefore|z|^{2}+|z-3|^{2}+|z-i|^{2} \begin{aligned}
=|$x+i y|^{2}+\mid &\mid x-3)+$\left.$i y\right|^{2} \\
&+|x+i(y-1)|^{2}
\end{aligned}

$=x^{2}+y^{2}+(x-3)^{2}+y^{2}+x^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=x^{2}+y^{2}+x^{2}-6 x+9+y^{2}+x^{2}+y^{2}=3 x^{2}+3 y^{2}-6 x-2 y+10=3\left(x^{2}-2 x+1\right)+3\left(y^{2}-\frac{2}{3} y+\frac{1}{9}\right)\quad=3(x-1)^{2}+3\left(y-\frac{1}{3}\right)^{2}+\frac{20}{3}$
It is minimum, when x-1=0 and $y-\frac{1}{3}=0\therefore \quad x=1 \quad and \quad y=\frac{1}{3}\therefore \quad z=1+\frac{1}{3} i$
